<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:lang="fr"><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="4.3.4">Jekyll</generator><link href="https://mohammedaissi.github.io/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml"/><link href="https://mohammedaissi.github.io/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="fr"/><updated>2026-04-18T15:15:02+00:00</updated><id>https://mohammedaissi.github.io/feed.xml</id><title type="html">Mohammed Aissi</title><subtitle>A simple, whitespace theme for academics. Based on [*folio](https://github.com/bogoli/-folio) design. </subtitle><entry><title type="html">STM32F411 Discovery — Circular LED Chaser with Speed Ramp</title><link href="https://mohammedaissi.github.io/blog/2025/formatting-and-links/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="STM32F411 Discovery — Circular LED Chaser with Speed Ramp"/><published>2025-09-07T00:40:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-09-07T00:40:00+00:00</updated><id>https://mohammedaissi.github.io/blog/2025/formatting-and-links</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://mohammedaissi.github.io/blog/2025/formatting-and-links/"><![CDATA[<p>This post shows how to control 4x user LEDs on the STM32F411 Discovery board <strong>(PD12 = <font color="green">GREEN</font>, PD13 = <font color="orange">ORANGE</font>, PD14 = <font color="red">RED</font>, PD15 = <font color="blue">BLUE</font>) in a **circular pattern</strong>:</p> <ul> <li>forward (clockwise),</li> <li>reverse (counter-clockwise),</li> <li>with speed variation (slow → fast → slow).</li> </ul> <style>.stm32-leds{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;margin:1rem 0}.stm32-leds .ring{position:relative;width:160px;height:160px;margin:.5rem auto}.stm32-leds .led{position:absolute;width:26px;height:26px;border-radius:50%;opacity:.25;box-shadow:0 0 0 currentColor;transform:scale(1.0);animation:blink var(--period,2.8s) infinite ease-in-out;animation-delay:calc(var(--i,0) * var(--step,.55s))}.pos0{top:0;left:calc(50% - 13px)}.pos1{top:calc(50% - 13px);right:0}.pos2{bottom:0;left:calc(50% - 13px)}.pos3{top:calc(50% - 13px);left:0}.pd12{color:#00c853;background:#00c853}.pd13{color:#ff9800;background:#ff9800}.pd14{color:#e53935;background:#e53935}.pd15{color:#1e88e5;background:#1e88e5}@keyframes blink{0%{opacity:.25;box-shadow:0 0 0 currentColor;transform:scale(1.00)}10%{opacity:1.00;box-shadow:0 0 16px currentColor;transform:scale(1.18)}25%{opacity:.25;box-shadow:0 0 0 currentColor;transform:scale(1.00)}100%{opacity:.25;box-shadow:0 0 0 currentColor;transform:scale(1.00)}}.stm32-leds.forward .pd12{--i:0}.stm32-leds.forward .pd13{--i:1}.stm32-leds.forward .pd14{--i:2}.stm32-leds.forward .pd15{--i:3}.stm32-leds.reverse .pd12{--i:0}.stm32-leds.reverse .pd15{--i:1}.stm32-leds.reverse .pd14{--i:2}.stm32-leds.reverse .pd13{--i:3}.legend{text-align:center;font-size:.9rem;opacity:.8}</style> <div style="display:flex; gap:160px; align-items:flex-start; flex-wrap:wrap;"> <div class="stm32-leds forward" style="--period:1.8s; --step:.55s;"> <div class="ring"> <div class="led pd12 pos0"></div> <div class="led pd13 pos1"></div> <div class="led pd14 pos2"></div> <div class="led pd15 pos3"></div> </div> <div class="legend">Forward (clockwise)</div> </div> <div class="stm32-leds reverse" style="--period:1.8s; --step:.55s;"> <div class="ring"> <div class="led pd12 pos0"></div> <div class="led pd13 pos1"></div> <div class="led pd14 pos2"></div> <div class="led pd15 pos3"></div> </div> <div class="legend">Reverse (counter-clockwise)</div> </div> </div> <div class="col-sm mt-8 mt-md-0"> <div style="max-width:420px;margin:0;"> <figure> <picture> <img src="/assets/img/blogs/STM32/stm32f411ve%20board.jpeg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> </div> <p>We use only <strong>register-level CMSIS</strong>, no <strong>HAL Hardware Abstraction Layer</strong>. <strong>What is CMSIS?</strong><br/> CMSIS (Cortex Microcontroller Software Interface Standard) is a set of low-level, vendor-independent C headers and functions for ARM Cortex microcontrollers. It lets you control hardware directly using registers.</p> <p><strong>What is HAL?</strong><br/> HAL (Hardware Abstraction Layer) is a higher-level library provided by chip vendors (like STMicroelectronics). It makes hardware control easier by hiding register details, but can be less efficient than CMSIS.</p> <p><a href="https://www.keil.arm.com/cmsis">Learn more about CMSIS in the official ARM documentation.</a></p> <hr/> <h2 id="full-code">Full code</h2> <div class="language-c highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="cp">#include</span> <span class="cpf">"stm32f4xx.h"</span><span class="cp">
</span>
<span class="cm">/* simple blocking delay */</span>
<span class="k">static</span> <span class="kt">void</span> <span class="nf">delay</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="k">volatile</span> <span class="kt">uint32_t</span> <span class="n">t</span><span class="p">){</span> <span class="k">while</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">t</span><span class="o">--</span><span class="p">);</span> <span class="p">}</span>

<span class="k">static</span> <span class="k">const</span> <span class="kt">uint8_t</span> <span class="n">pins</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="mi">4</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="p">{</span><span class="mi">12</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="mi">13</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="mi">14</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="mi">15</span><span class="p">};</span>   <span class="c1">// PD12..PD15</span>

<span class="cm">/* blink one full ramp cycle in given direction: +1=FWD, -1=REV */</span>
<span class="k">static</span> <span class="kt">void</span> <span class="nf">run_cycle</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="kt">int</span> <span class="n">dir</span><span class="p">){</span>
  <span class="kt">uint32_t</span> <span class="n">t_max</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="mi">800000</span><span class="p">;</span>   <span class="c1">// slow</span>
  <span class="kt">uint32_t</span> <span class="n">t_min</span> <span class="o">=</span>  <span class="mi">80000</span><span class="p">;</span>   <span class="c1">// fast</span>
  <span class="kt">uint32_t</span> <span class="n">step</span>   <span class="o">=</span>  <span class="mi">40000</span><span class="p">;</span>  <span class="c1">// ramp step</span>

  <span class="kt">int</span> <span class="n">idx</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="p">(</span><span class="n">dir</span><span class="o">&gt;</span><span class="mi">0</span><span class="p">)</span><span class="o">?</span><span class="mi">0</span><span class="o">:</span><span class="mi">3</span><span class="p">;</span>

  <span class="cm">/* SLOW -&gt; FAST */</span>
  <span class="k">for</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="kt">uint32_t</span> <span class="n">t</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="n">t_max</span><span class="p">;</span> <span class="n">t</span><span class="o">&gt;=</span><span class="n">t_min</span><span class="p">;</span> <span class="n">t</span><span class="o">-=</span><span class="n">step</span><span class="p">){</span>
    <span class="n">GPIOD</span><span class="o">-&gt;</span><span class="n">BSRRL</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">1u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="n">pins</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="n">idx</span><span class="p">]);</span>   <span class="c1">// ON</span>
    <span class="n">delay</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">t</span><span class="p">);</span>
    <span class="n">GPIOD</span><span class="o">-&gt;</span><span class="n">BSRRH</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">1u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="n">pins</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="n">idx</span><span class="p">]);</span>   <span class="c1">// OFF</span>

    <span class="k">if</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">dir</span><span class="o">&gt;</span><span class="mi">0</span><span class="p">){</span> <span class="n">idx</span><span class="o">++</span><span class="p">;</span> <span class="k">if</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">idx</span><span class="o">==</span><span class="mi">4</span><span class="p">)</span> <span class="n">idx</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">0</span><span class="p">;</span> <span class="p">}</span>
    <span class="k">else</span>     <span class="p">{</span> <span class="k">if</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">idx</span><span class="o">==</span><span class="mi">0</span><span class="p">)</span> <span class="n">idx</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">3</span><span class="p">;</span> <span class="k">else</span> <span class="n">idx</span><span class="o">--</span><span class="p">;</span> <span class="p">}</span>
  <span class="p">}</span>

  <span class="cm">/* FAST -&gt; SLOW */</span>
  <span class="k">for</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="kt">uint32_t</span> <span class="n">t</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="n">t_min</span><span class="p">;</span> <span class="n">t</span><span class="o">&lt;=</span><span class="n">t_max</span><span class="p">;</span> <span class="n">t</span><span class="o">+=</span><span class="n">step</span><span class="p">){</span>
    <span class="n">GPIOD</span><span class="o">-&gt;</span><span class="n">BSRRL</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">1u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="n">pins</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="n">idx</span><span class="p">]);</span>   <span class="c1">// ON</span>
    <span class="n">delay</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">t</span><span class="p">);</span>
    <span class="n">GPIOD</span><span class="o">-&gt;</span><span class="n">BSRRH</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">1u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="n">pins</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="n">idx</span><span class="p">]);</span>   <span class="c1">// OFF</span>

    <span class="k">if</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">dir</span><span class="o">&gt;</span><span class="mi">0</span><span class="p">){</span> <span class="n">idx</span><span class="o">++</span><span class="p">;</span> <span class="k">if</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">idx</span><span class="o">==</span><span class="mi">4</span><span class="p">)</span> <span class="n">idx</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">0</span><span class="p">;</span> <span class="p">}</span>
    <span class="k">else</span>     <span class="p">{</span> <span class="k">if</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">idx</span><span class="o">==</span><span class="mi">0</span><span class="p">)</span> <span class="n">idx</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">3</span><span class="p">;</span> <span class="k">else</span> <span class="n">idx</span><span class="o">--</span><span class="p">;</span> <span class="p">}</span>
  <span class="p">}</span>
<span class="p">}</span>

<span class="kt">int</span> <span class="nf">main</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="kt">void</span><span class="p">){</span>
  <span class="cm">/* 1) Enable GPIOD clock */</span>
  <span class="n">RCC</span><span class="o">-&gt;</span><span class="n">AHB1ENR</span> <span class="o">|=</span> <span class="n">RCC_AHB1ENR_GPIODEN</span><span class="p">;</span>

  <span class="cm">/* 2) Configure PD12..PD15 as outputs (MODER bits = 01) */</span>
  <span class="n">GPIOD</span><span class="o">-&gt;</span><span class="n">MODER</span> <span class="o">&amp;=</span> <span class="o">~</span><span class="p">((</span><span class="mi">3u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">12</span><span class="o">*</span><span class="mi">2</span><span class="p">))</span><span class="o">|</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">3u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">13</span><span class="o">*</span><span class="mi">2</span><span class="p">))</span><span class="o">|</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">3u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">14</span><span class="o">*</span><span class="mi">2</span><span class="p">))</span><span class="o">|</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">3u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">15</span><span class="o">*</span><span class="mi">2</span><span class="p">)));</span>
  <span class="n">GPIOD</span><span class="o">-&gt;</span><span class="n">MODER</span> <span class="o">|=</span>  <span class="p">((</span><span class="mi">1u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">12</span><span class="o">*</span><span class="mi">2</span><span class="p">))</span><span class="o">|</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">1u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">13</span><span class="o">*</span><span class="mi">2</span><span class="p">))</span><span class="o">|</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">1u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">14</span><span class="o">*</span><span class="mi">2</span><span class="p">))</span><span class="o">|</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">1u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">15</span><span class="o">*</span><span class="mi">2</span><span class="p">)));</span>

  <span class="k">while</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">1</span><span class="p">){</span>
    <span class="n">run_cycle</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="o">+</span><span class="mi">1</span><span class="p">);</span>   <span class="c1">// forward: PD12→PD13→PD14→PD15</span>
    <span class="n">run_cycle</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="o">-</span><span class="mi">1</span><span class="p">);</span>   <span class="c1">// reverse: PD15→PD14→PD13→PD12</span>
  <span class="p">}</span>
<span class="p">}</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <hr/> <h2 id="explanation-with-bitwise-examples">Explanation with bitwise examples</h2> <h3 id="enable-clock-for-port-d">Enable clock for port D</h3> <div class="language-c highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="n">RCC</span><span class="o">-&gt;</span><span class="n">AHB1ENR</span> <span class="o">|=</span> <span class="n">RCC_AHB1ENR_GPIODEN</span><span class="p">;</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <ul> <li><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">RCC_AHB1ENR_GPIODEN = (1&lt;&lt;3)</code></li> <li>If <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">R = 0000 0000</code> (binary low 8 bits),<br/> after operation: <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">R = 0000 1000</code>.</li> </ul> <h3 id="configure-pd12pd15-as-outputs">Configure PD12..PD15 as outputs</h3> <div class="language-c highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="n">GPIOD</span><span class="o">-&gt;</span><span class="n">MODER</span> <span class="o">&amp;=</span> <span class="o">~</span><span class="p">((</span><span class="mi">3u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">12</span><span class="o">*</span><span class="mi">2</span><span class="p">))</span><span class="o">|</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">3u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">13</span><span class="o">*</span><span class="mi">2</span><span class="p">))</span><span class="o">|</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">3u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">14</span><span class="o">*</span><span class="mi">2</span><span class="p">))</span><span class="o">|</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">3u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">15</span><span class="o">*</span><span class="mi">2</span><span class="p">)));</span>
<span class="n">GPIOD</span><span class="o">-&gt;</span><span class="n">MODER</span> <span class="o">|=</span>  <span class="p">((</span><span class="mi">1u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">12</span><span class="o">*</span><span class="mi">2</span><span class="p">))</span><span class="o">|</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">1u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">13</span><span class="o">*</span><span class="mi">2</span><span class="p">))</span><span class="o">|</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">1u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">14</span><span class="o">*</span><span class="mi">2</span><span class="p">))</span><span class="o">|</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">1u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">15</span><span class="o">*</span><span class="mi">2</span><span class="p">)));</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <ul> <li>Each pin uses 2 bits in <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">MODER</code>: <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">00=input</code>, <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">01=output</code>.</li> <li>Example for PD12: bits <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">[25:24]</code>.</li> <li>Binary clear: <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">..00..</code> then set: <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">..01..</code>.</li> </ul> <h3 id="turn-led-on">Turn LED ON</h3> <div class="language-c highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="n">GPIOD</span><span class="o">-&gt;</span><span class="n">BSRRL</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">1u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="mi">12</span><span class="p">);</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <ul> <li><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">BSRRL</code> low half sets bits = 1.</li> <li>If <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">ODR=0000 0000 0000</code>, after: <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">ODR=0001 0000 0000 0000</code>.</li> </ul> <h3 id="turn-led-off">Turn LED OFF</h3> <div class="language-c highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="n">GPIOD</span><span class="o">-&gt;</span><span class="n">BSRRH</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">1u</span><span class="o">&lt;&lt;</span><span class="mi">12</span><span class="p">);</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <ul> <li><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">BSRRH</code> high half clears bits = 1.</li> <li>If <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">ODR=0001 0000 0000 0000</code>, after: <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">ODR=0000 0000 0000 0000</code>.</li> </ul> <h3 id="delay">Delay</h3> <div class="language-c highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="n">delay</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">t</span><span class="p">);</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <ul> <li>Simple busy-loop, <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">t</code> controls speed.</li> <li>In our loop: decreases (<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">t_max→t_min</code>) for faster, then increases for slower.</li> </ul> <hr/> <h2 id="behavior">Behavior</h2> <ol> <li>All LEDs chase in a circle: Green → Orange → Red → Blue.</li> <li>Speed ramps from <strong>slow → fast → slow</strong>.</li> <li>Direction reverses: Blue → Red → Orange → Green.</li> <li>Pattern repeats infinitely.</li> </ol> <hr/> <blockquote> <p>⚠️ Note: If your CMSIS headers define unified <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">BSRR</code>, replace:</p> <ul> <li>ON → <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">GPIOD-&gt;BSRR = (1u&lt;&lt;pin);</code></li> <li>OFF → <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">GPIOD-&gt;BSRR = (1u&lt;&lt;(pin+16));</code></li> </ul> </blockquote>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="sample-posts"/><category term="formatting"/><category term="links"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Bare-metal GPIO example — LEDs PD12..PD15 chasing forward and reverse with slow→fast→slow pattern]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">a post with code</title><link href="https://mohammedaissi.github.io/blog/2015/code/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="a post with code"/><published>2015-07-15T15:09:00+00:00</published><updated>2015-07-15T15:09:00+00:00</updated><id>https://mohammedaissi.github.io/blog/2015/code</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://mohammedaissi.github.io/blog/2015/code/"><![CDATA[<div class="language-c++ highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="n">Q1</span><span class="p">)</span> <span class="n">Why</span> <span class="n">are</span> <span class="n">addresses</span> <span class="n">written</span> <span class="n">in</span> <span class="n">HEX</span> <span class="n">but</span> <span class="n">declared</span> <span class="n">as</span> <span class="kt">uint32_t</span><span class="o">?</span>
<span class="o">-</span> <span class="n">HEX</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">just</span> <span class="n">a</span> <span class="n">human</span><span class="o">-</span><span class="n">friendly</span> <span class="n">representation</span> <span class="p">(</span><span class="n">groups</span> <span class="n">of</span> <span class="mi">4</span> <span class="n">bits</span> <span class="n">per</span> <span class="n">hex</span> <span class="n">digit</span><span class="p">).</span>
